WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.765
This is the photograph I kept after trying to section a

00:00:04.765 --> 00:00:07.903
zebrafish specimen. The block fragmented. There was no

00:00:07.903 --> 00:00:09.079
slide to interpret.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.057
The specimens were tiny. A small change in orientation

00:00:18.057 --> 00:00:21.264
could decide whether a section passed through the

00:00:21.264 --> 00:00:24.069
anatomy I needed, or missed it entirely.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:34.585
My plan was to hold each specimen in a two percent

00:00:34.585 --> 00:00:37.386
agarose matrix. That support would establish

00:00:37.386 --> 00:00:39.721
orientation before subsequent tissue processing.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:48.302
After dehydration and clearing, paraffin was meant to

00:00:48.302 --> 00:00:51.672
provide sufficient mechanical support for microtomy. On

00:00:51.672 --> 00:00:55.042
paper, each material had a reasonable job.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:04.069
The agarose–paraffin interface deserves scrutiny, but a

00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:08.205
photograph of separating layers does not identify the

00:01:08.205 --> 00:01:09.239
molecular cause.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.871
The processed block formed distinguishable layers. At

00:01:17.871 --> 00:01:22.269
the microtome, they separated and broke apart. A usable

00:01:22.269 --> 00:01:25.201
ribbon of histological sections never appeared.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.251
The failure involved the materials, not simply the

00:01:36.251 --> 00:01:40.527
machine. But what I could observe was separation. Its

00:01:40.527 --> 00:01:42.903
precise physical explanation remained unresolved.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:52.202
The grade and thermal behaviour of agarose might have

00:01:52.202 --> 00:01:55.120
contributed. I did not establish that experimentally,

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.038
and the photographs alone cannot prove it.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.327
A future test could vary the agarose grade and

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:10.343
processing conditions, then check whether the block

00:02:10.343 --> 00:02:11.205
sections intact.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.189
No usable section emerged. I kept the fragments and

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:23.512
photographs so the next experiment begins with what

00:02:23.512 --> 00:02:23.927
failed.
